Dear Yves,

>                  ELDIR ~ a*SNFE
>                  ELDIP ~ d*SNFE

Basically, through these two lines I wanted to show that in my model ELDIR and ELDIP are mediators which are influenced by independent reflective 2nd order factor SNFE. Does this syntax make sense then?

As I have read in previous treads in this group, usually only formative factors were used as independent ones, do you believe it will be possible to do otherwise?

I attach the diagram for better understanding.

Artem

On Fri, Jul 31, 2020 at 5:40 PM Yves Rosseel <yros...@gmail.com> wrote:

> On 7/31/20 11:26 AM, ZADOROZHNYY, ARTEM wrote:
> >                   ELDIR <~ ELDIR2 + ELDIR4 + ELDIR5 + ELDIR7 + ELDIR8
> >                   ELDIP <~ ELDIP1 + ELDIP2 + ELDIP3 + ELDIP4 + ELDIP6
>
> Perhaps this is done automatically (not sure), but I would fix the scale
> as follows:
>
>    ELDIR <~ 1*ELDIR2 + ELDIR4 + ELDIR5 + ELDIR7 + ELDIR8
>    ELDIP <~ 1*ELDIP1 + ELDIP2 + ELDIP3 + ELDIP4 + ELDIP6
>
> >                  ELDIR ~ a*SNFE
> >                  ELDIP ~ d*SNFE
>
> This two lines look strange to me: SNFE is now just another 'indicator'
> of the formative constructs ELDIR/ELDIP
>
> >                  WTC ~ c*SNFE + b*ELDIR + e*ELDIP
>
> Yes, this is what need (I think): ELDIR/ELDIP must be predictors in an
> regression equation.
>
> Yves.
