From: Terrence Jorgensen
Sent: Thursday, July 30, 2020 8:46 AM
To: lavaan
Subject: Re: Can I generate data for path model with only observed variables by simulateData function

>
> there are only three choices in model.type, which are “cfa”, “sem” and “growth”

Those are arbitrary.  See the help-page description for what they affect (not the data generation).  Here is an example:

model <- ' # direct effect
             Y ~ .5*X
           # mediator
             M ~ 0.5*X
             Y ~ 0.5*M
           # (residual) variances
             X ~~ 1*X
             M ~~ 0.75*M
             Y ~~ 0.25*Y
'
fitted(sem(model))
simulateData(model, sample.nobs = 5)

>
> skewness and kurtosis can be apply to all observed variables (all 5 variables in my case, but I only want to apply to 4 of them).

So set those to 0 for the fifth variable.

Terrence D. Jorgensen

