Hi,

I would like to get bootstrapped CIs for my estimates (especially a total and an indirect effect in a mediation model), but I need to use a robust estimator (mlm) because of non-normality of the data.

Is there a possibility to do both at the same time? se = "bootstrap" and estimator = "mlm" does not work at the same time. I tried to first estimate the lavaan object with mlm and afterwards bootstrap SE/CIs with the bootstrapLavaan() function. It works, but I don't get the values for the total1 (total1 := c1 + (a1 * b1)) and indirect1 (indirect1 := a1 * b1), only the values for a1, b1 and c1.

Can I specify something in the bootstrapLavaan()-function to also bootstrap indirect1 and total1? Or is there another possibility I am missing?

Best,
Michael

