Constraining factor variances is not part of invariance testing. The variances may, in fact, differ naturally and correctly between the two times if responses are converging or diverging over time.

That said, std.lv <http://std.lv>=TRUE is also not appropriate for invariance testing precisely because of the above. It forces actual differences in the factor variances to manifest in the loadings or (if loadings are constrained) residuals.

Since you used std.lv <http://std.lv>=TRUE, constraining the latent variances doesn't affect fit since the variances are both forced to 1 and therefore already equal.

Pat

