Strict invariance: My understanding was there are two "levels" of strict invariance, one being factor variances and the other being item residuals. I'll look into this more, though. In the meantime, I've changed to "resid.autocov" instead of "lv.autocov" for now.

std.lv <http://std.lv>: I looked into the Kloessner & Klopp (2019) paper about methods for identifying common-factor variances. Regardless, I tried all three ID.fac methods and none of them change the results: there is no difference between the strong and strict invariance models.

Dana

