> Joe, thank you for the response and the references. I have read the material about centering and have used in the past. Do you think one needs to group-mean center the variables before creating the interaction even if we focus only on the within-level?

You are welcome.  Hesitant to say without knowing more about the design and measurement. Why not try it both ways and see what happens?

>
> Regarding MPLUS and Preacher et al. reference, I had used it as a guide in my initial post. Can you please check whether the implementation makes sense? This thread can be a nice guide for other researchers who may be interested in looking at both levels even in 1-1-1 models.

I think so, though I'm not sure about the computation of the conditional effects. I take it you've seen the "Figure it out" website that converts Process-based conditionals to Mplus?  It's been quite helpful and you should be able to find your model there: http://offbeat.group.shef.ac.uk/FIO/mplusmedmod.htm.  Fairly simple to convert the Mplus equations to lavaan.

>
> Finally, are you familiar with a way to plot the first stage interaction effect (eg semPlots?).

Not off hand, though there's an R package called "interaction" that might help.  See: https://cran.r-project.org/web/packages/interactions/index.html

>
> Thank you for your time and help.

You are welcome.  Wish I could be of more help.  I've run into many of the issues along the way and it just takes a bit of digging and perseverance.

Joe

