Hayley, for what it's worth, simulation studies suggest that in this situation, with exchangeable level 1 observations and the outcome at level 2, you don't lose much by simply aggregating (e.g., averaging) the level 1 values into a level 2 "observed" variable and running the resulting level-2 variables as a single-level model.

