> > In order to test the unique contribution of PS as a moderator, I wanted to compare the main model of interest with two other models including each potential moderator using the model chi square, the CFI and RMSEA to evaluate goodness-of-fit.
>
> In order for models to be comparable, they need to be fit to the same variables (including interaction terms).  So you would need to include all moderators in each model, and take turns fixing effects of different moderators to zero.  Then models can be compared, but only using fit measures that do not require nesting, such as information criteria (e.g., AIC, BIC) and incremental fit indices (e.g., CFI, TLI).
