> The number of free parameters are 14 (lavaan) and 42 (mplus) and this difference is due to lavaan not reporting SEs for any of the item thresholds (14*2 = 28).

It is related to that, but not caused by it.  When you use the base lavaan() function rather than the sem() or cfa() wrappers, you only estimate the parameters explicitly specified in your model syntax.

pcString <- '
pc =~ PC1_1 + PC1_2 + PC1_3 + PC1_4 + PC1_5 + PC1_6 + PC1_7 + PC1_8 + PC1_9 + PC2_1 + PC2_3 + PC3_1 + PC3_2 + PC3_3

pc ~~ 1.0*pc
pc ~ 0*1
'
m.pcFit <- lavaan(pcString, data = analyticSamp, ordered = pcItems, parameterization = "theta", mimic = "mplus")

You could set auto.th <http://auto.th> = TRUE (which is what the sem() and cfa() wrappers do) or specify your thresholds in the model syntax to set them free in your model.

Terrence D. Jorgensen
Assistant Professor, Methods and Statistics
Research Institute for Child Development and Education, the University of Amsterdam
http://www.uva.nl/profile/t.d.jorgensen

